    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The Yosemite 15-minute quadrangle lies on the western slope of the central Sierra Nevada, California, between altitudes of about 800 and 3000 m. Most of the quadrangle is within Yosemite National Park. This report supplements the geologic map of the Yosemite quadrangle, central Sierra Nevada, California, which was published in the U.S. Geological Survey’s Geologic Investigations Series as I–2751. This report presents modal, chemical, and isotopic data on \r\nplutonic rocks from the Yosemite quadrangle. The locations of the samples are plotted on a topographic map of the quadrangle accompanying this report.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
